; TEST: abort=1
;
; u8 3 - 5 = -2: below the bottom of u8. The raw 64-bit difference is
; 2^64 - 2; normalised to u8 it is 254.
; Abort kind 1, the numeric trap (prelude/README.md) -- the shared
; `bfausr_trap`. If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; This one does borrow in 64 bits, but below 64 the emitter consults no flag
; for `sub` either (for an iN the borrow would mean nothing): it compares the
; difference with its normalised copy, as for `add` (ssa-ir.md 2.2).
;
; Mutation (run): the trapping form emitted as the wrapping one (no
; compare) -> exit 7.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u8 3
%2 = iconst u8 5
%3 = sub u8 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
